# SNIP architecture (this repository)

This repo is the first **SNIP domain application** (Network Planning & Optimisation), not the entire Simba Network Intelligence Platform.

Read before changing code:

- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-CONTEXT.md` (section 0 is authoritative for scope)
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-STATUS.md`
- `docs/architecture/SNIP-PHASE-7-MULTI-VENDOR-NETWORK-INTEGRATION-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-PHASE-7-MULTI-VENDOR-NETWORK-INTEGRATION-SPECIFICATION.md`

Root copies also exist:

- `SNIP-PHASE-7-MULTI-VENDOR-NETWORK-INTEGRATION-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `SNIP-PHASE-7-MULTI-VENDOR-NETWORK-INTEGRATION-SPECIFICATION.md`

## Authorised now

Phase **7** is architecturally accepted and **frozen** on the Phase 6 baseline (`9c8d57b600f3bc8f9d251767211985a550502e5d`). Do not add Phase 7 functionality, resolve deferred technical debt, or refactor for its own sake.

Preserve Phase 1A/1A.1/1B/2/3/4/5/6/7. Kafka remains off by default. Do not vectorize operational telemetry, imported operational records, or Assurance Case state. Detection remains deterministic. The LLM explains and prioritises investigation; it does not decide thresholds, severity, confidence, risk, policy, numeric simulation results, or reconciliation outcomes. AI may propose. Deterministic policy decides. Humans approve where required. MCP invokes only registered capabilities.

Exactly one Chief Orchestration Agent plus Knowledge, Context, Assurance, and Decision specialists. Communication is orchestrator-mediated. Orchestration is synchronous and bounded. Persist structured AgentPlan / PlanStep only; no hidden chain-of-thought. Memory is ephemeral Run Memory, concise Case Memory, and existing Enterprise Memory. Agent Registry is in-code. Permissions are explicit least privilege. One shared physical LLM initially; AgentModelResolver is retained; no heterogeneous model routing. Agents reuse Phase 4 ProposedAction. Phase 4 remains authoritative for risk, policy, approval, execution, MCP, and action audit. Agents have no direct MCP or network execution authority. No Digital Twin Agent or Vendor Integration Agent is added.

Phase 6 remains frozen: cell-centric versioned Digital Twin; manual/on-demand sync; CURRENT/STALE/EXPIRED freshness; txPower-only registry; deterministic synthetic model. Governed simulation execution remains Phase 4 → human approval → MCP `simulation.cell-parameter.v1` → Digital Twin simulation. Do not expose an ungoverned public simulate endpoint. Do not automatically synchronize on Kafka/telemetry or vendor import. STALE/EXPIRED twins must not simulate.

Phase 7 remains frozen: fixture-first, read-only Ericsson and Nokia inventory/topology/configuration integration. Vendor specificity ends at the adapter boundary. SNIP owns canonical IDs. Reconciliation is deterministic (CREATE / UPDATE / UNCHANGED / CONFLICT / REJECT) with one authoritative source per entity and no vendor precedence. Entity/snapshot-level provenance is sufficient; field-level provenance is deferred. Import replay may create a new batch while canonical state stays idempotent. Complete snapshots may mark previously seen source entities MISSING; partial snapshots must not; missing entities are not physically deleted. STALE/EXPIRED twins must not simulate. Import must **not** call `TwinSynchronizationService`. Do not connect to real ENM/NetAct. Do not add vendor write methods, vendor MCP tools, vendor telemetry adapters, automatic conflict resolution, mastership policy engines, raw payload archives, or continuous/incremental import.

Same-JVM loopback JSON-RPC HTTP MCP remains accepted. Phase 4 POST APIs mutate SNIP governance state only. Agent-run POST APIs mutate SNIP orchestration state only. Twin-management POST APIs mutate SNIP Twin/scenario state only. Twin-management and integration POST APIs do not authorise live network mutation. Failed-result row replacement remains deferred technical debt. Non-interruptible per-Agent timeout is accepted Phase 5 technical debt; preserve the future interruptible timeout / run watchdog requirement and do not redesign it. Failed Twin simulation attempts are not persisted as SimulationRun records; that remains accepted Phase 6 technical debt. Absence of distributed import locking is an accepted Phase 7 limitation.

Governance POST APIs mutate SNIP workflow state only. They must never write to the live network. Direct LLM-to-MCP invocation is prohibited. Direct Agent-to-MCP invocation is prohibited. The LLM must not produce authoritative numeric KPI predictions.

## Do not implement

Agent Factory, dynamic Agent creation, self-modifying Agents, persistent conversational memory, long-running or continuous background Agents, freeform Agent-to-Agent mesh, automatic remediation, Agent approval authority, policy override, production Agent identity federation, different physical models per Agent, automatic model routing, live OSS/NMS/EMS integrations, live gNB/network writes, Ericsson ENM / Nokia NetAct connectivity or writes, incident-management / ITSM, Schema Registry, Avro, Protobuf, Flink, Spark, Kafka Streams, dedicated time-series DB, EKS/Kubernetes, Kong, ALB, ALICE, RL, ML anomaly detection, adaptive thresholds, forecasting, billing, Ionic, AWS lock-in, production IAM/OIDC, remote third-party MCP, vendor MCP adapters, production RF simulation, ray tracing, vendor-calibrated radio models, electricalTilt simulation, arbitrary parameter simulation, automatic optimization, best-parameter search, whole-network Twin, core-network Twin, transport Twin, remote vendor Digital Twin, Kafka-triggered automatic Twin synchronization, continuous Twin synchronization, graph database, 3D GIS Twin, mobility simulation, traffic forecasting, network rollback, vendor REST/SFTP/SNMP/NETCONF/gNMI/Bulk CM, vendor telemetry streaming, automatic conflict resolution, AI reconciliation, dynamic adapter plugins, raw payload DB archive, field-level provenance, mastership policy engine, continuous/incremental import, Vendor Integration Agent, Phase 8.

## Rules

- Extend Phase 1A/1B/2/3/4/5/6 abstractions. Do not rewrite the slice.
- Keep recommendation and domain APIs read-only for the network. Action execute/approve mutate SNIP governance state only. Agent-run POST APIs mutate SNIP orchestration state only. Twin synchronize/scenario APIs mutate SNIP Twin state only. Integration import APIs mutate SNIP integration/operational state only.
- If retrieval is empty, do not fabricate citations or specialist evidence.
- Ordinary CI must not download large models. PostgreSQL via Testcontainers remains required. Kafka Testcontainers remains allowed.
- Implementation markdown lives under `docs/implementation/`. ADRs under `docs/architecture/adr/`.
- Architecture document has architectural authority. Implementation specification is the authorised execution scope.
- Do not push or establish a new Git baseline until asked after Phase 7 architectural acceptance.
